        "original_id": "39d2adc4-1291-59d4-8bfc-28adb3e42329",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1820 Maine gubernatorial election, Maine statehood\n- People: William King\n- Places: Maine, Massachusetts, Bath\n- Concepts: Missouri Compromise\n\nFacts:\n- Maine was recognized as a state on March 15, 1820, after separating from Massachusetts.\n- Maine's separation from Massachusetts came as a result of the Missouri Compromise.\n- The 1820 Maine gubernatorial election was the first election for Governor of Maine.\n- The 1820 Maine gubernatorial election resulted in the virtually unanimous election of William King.\n- William King was chiefly responsible for the push for Maine statehood.\n- William King was born on February 9, 1768, and died on June 17, 1852.\n- William King was an American merchant, shipbuilder, army officer, and statesman from Bath, Maine.",
